info:
The Royal Hospital School does NOT appoint guardians on behalf of parents. 

The nominated guardian must:
 be over 25 years of age;
 be a permanent resident of the United Kingdom;
 reside within 2 hours travelling distance from the School, either by car or public transport;
 be a 24 hour point of contact for pupil, parents and the School;
 not be a member of staff at the Royal Hospital School
 act with delegated parental authority in the case of emergency or in other matters as required;
 provide appropriate overnight accommodation, if required, including at the start and end of terms and half terms.
Guardians
